---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Sheet from "../components/Sheet.astro";
import { profile } from "../data/profile";
---

<Base title="About - Varun Malhotra">
  <Sheet rail={false}>
    <h1
      class="u-display page-title"
    >
      About
    </h1>

    <div class="about-intro">
      <p>
        The through-line has been the same question in different clothes: how do you know the
        model is right. At Samsung it was image restoration you could judge by eye. At Michelin it
        is a natural-language interface to a pricing warehouse, where the answer looks equally
        plausible whether or not it is correct, and eyeballing it stops working.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is why most of what I build now is evaluation and guardrails rather than models.
        Benchmarks that exist before the system does, read-only enforcement that holds at every
        layer, gates that stop the agent when it is uncertain instead of letting it guess
        confidently.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am in {profile.location}, and I am looking for work where the system has to hold up
        under real users rather than a demo.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="rule section-rule" />

    <h2
      class="u-label section-heading"
    >
      Positions
    </h2>
    <div>
      {
        profile.roles.map((r) => (
          <div class="list-row">
            <span class="fig list-row-date">
              {r.dates}
            </span>
            <span class="list-row-main">
              <span class="list-row-title">
                {r.title}
              </span>
              {r.current && <span class="status-mark"> ●</span>}
              <br />
              <span class="list-row-sub">{r.company}</span>
            </span>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <hr class="rule section-rule" />

    <h2
      class="u-label section-heading"
    >
      Education
    </h2>
    <div class="list-row">
      <span class="fig list-row-date">
        {profile.education.dates}
      </span>
      <span class="list-row-main">
        <span class="list-row-title">
          {profile.education.school}
        </span>
        <br />
        <span class="list-row-sub">
          {profile.education.degree}, GPA {profile.education.gpa}
        </span>
      </span>
    </div>

    <hr class="rule section-rule" />

    <h2
      class="u-label section-heading"
    >
      Skills
    </h2>
    <div class="skills-list">
      {
        profile.skills.map((g) => (
          <p class="skills-group">
            <span class="u-label skills-group-label">{g.group}:</span>{" "}
            {g.items.map((s, i) => (
              <Fragment>
                {i > 0 && <span class="pipe-sep"> ❘ </span>}
                <span class="skills-item">{s}</span>
              </Fragment>
            ))}
          </p>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <hr class="rule section-rule" />

    <h2
      class="u-label section-heading"
    >
      Contact
    </h2>
    <p class="contact-block">
      <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`} class="link-underline">{profile.email}</a><br />
      <a href={profile.linkedin} class="link-underline">{profile.linkedin.replace("https://www.", "")}</a><br />
      <a href={profile.github} class="link-underline">{profile.github.replace("https://", "")}</a><br />
      <span class="text-muted">{profile.location}</span>
    </p>
  </Sheet>
</Base>
